`preventOrphans` uses ordinary spaces to identify the final two words, so reuse it for English only. Japanese and Thai need locale-aware segmentation; this helper cannot guarantee that their final word won’t wrap alone.

```dart
String formatHeading(String text, Locale locale) {
  return locale.languageCode == 'en'
      ? preventOrphans(text)
      : text;
}
```

For Japanese and Thai, use translator-approved non-breaking groups or locale-aware line-breaking logic. Even English needs narrow-width checks when the final pair is wider than the container.

Verify localized headings at narrow widths and 1.5×/2× text scaling, including empty and long copy. Widget tests should check for overflow, intended line counts, and English non-breaking pairing.
